From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:30:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 60/60] feat(canvas): a frame waiting for its picture shows a
 placeholder, not a white box

A frame that is neither a live document nor showing its picture yet was a
plain white box: indistinguishable from an empty design, for as long as the
picture took to arrive or the server took to draw it (seconds on the first
look after an edit, until the previous patch draws it ahead).

FramePreview now shows, under the picture, the pulse every placeholder in the
app uses (Skeleton's bg-paper-deep with skeleton-pulse), starting after 300 ms
so a picture that arrives sooner never shows it, and gone once the picture is
decoded. It is one endless, delayed animation: a finite fade-in is cancelled
when the picture arrives, and its rejected `finished` broke code awaiting the
page's animations. A picture whose last retry failed too (a render that failed, a
signed-out visitor past the render budget) says so instead of staying white:
'No picture of this frame yet. Select it to open it.', at a constant size on
screen; selecting it makes it a live document. Canvas elements, which have no
picture, are unchanged.
